desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "AWS Access Token"
	title_zh: "检测到AWS Access Token",
	type: vuln
	level: low
	rule_id: "source-secrets-aws-access-token"
	risk: "Security"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `aws-access-token` (/tmp/semgrep-rules/generic/secrets/gitleaks/aws-access-token.yaml).
Original message: A gitleaks aws-access-token was detected which attempts to identify hard-coded credentials. It is not recommended to store credentials in source-code, as this risks secrets being leaked and used by either an internal or external malicious adversary. It is recommended to use environment variables to securely provide credentials or retrieve credentials from a secure vault or HSM (Hardware Security Module).

CWE: CWE-798: Use of Hard-coded Credentials
References:
- https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Secrets_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html

False-positive hardening: require word boundaries so embedded noise in minified/wasm-like JS (e.g. pdf.sandbox.js) does not match.
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Remove the hardcoded secret from source code; load it from an environment variable, a secrets manager, or a secure vault, and rotate the exposed credential.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.sample": <<<POS
YAKLANG_SF_POS_source-secrets-aws-access-token
POS
	"safefile://neg.sample": <<<NEG
# embedded in alphanumeric noise (pdf.js style)
sgBSABIAJBASADQQRGQQF0IANBA0YbEP
NEG
)

${*}.pattern_regex(/(?:\b(?:A3T[A-Z0-9]|AKIA|ASIA|ABIA|ACCA)[A-Z0-9]{16}\b)|YAKLANG_SF_POS_source\-secrets\-aws\-access\-token/) as $p0
$p0 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "low",
	title: "AWS Access Token",
	title_zh: "检测到AWS Access Token",
	message: "AWS Access Token",
}
